//! {{ c.names }} behind `can[]` ({{ "indices " ~ (c.chans | map(attribute="index") | join(", ")) if many else "index 0" }}): the task that owns each
//! controller (the `mcan` driver), the queues between it and the WireWeaver server (`src/ww/can.rs`), the
//! transceiver's standby pin.
//!
//! The tasks run on their own interrupt executor ([start], {{ c.executor }}), above the server and USB, and are woken by
//! the FDCAN interrupts. Each moves received frames into its [Chan::rx], puts what the server queued in [Chan::tx]
//! into the transmit FIFO, and is the only one that switches its controller's mode ([command]). What is lost on the
//! way is counted ([Chan::rx_lost], `cnt` counters). The server reads the status directly ([status], through mcan's
//! `StatusReader`); [WAKE] tells it there are frames or credit to pass on.
//!
//! The checks of host input and the mappings are in `bedrock_can` (host-tested); this module only turns them into
//! mcan calls. Ported from the B135 firmware (vb135_fdcan_iso_usb_fw `b135_fw/src/can.rs`).

